# Normalise line endings on the way in and check out LF everywhere.
#
# The test suite compares recovered program text against fixtures, and the GACPD
# parsers are line-oriented. Letting Git for Windows convert to CRLF on checkout
# would make that text differ by platform, so a fixture that matches on Linux
# would not match on Windows for reasons that have nothing to do with the code.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything read as bytes, or whose exact bytes are the point.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
*.jar binary
*.patch -text
*.diff -text
